messages.text:
You're right, that's my slip. After my context was compacted I stopped passing the agent's name when starting new agents. Three recent agents went out unnamed: the test-speed toolsmith (done), the new ops hub, and the toolsmith for the Safari 'open after park' problem. Why it matters: other agents can't message an unnamed agent by name, so messages route through me.
Why 'general-purpose': the project's own agent roles (toolsmith, fix-owner, reviewer…) only load when a session starts. Mid-session I start each one as a general-purpose agent and tell it to read its role file first. The role is the same; only the label differs. A fresh session shows the real role names.
Fix now:
- the ops hub is replaced by a named one, mgmt-ops-9, so peers can reach it;
- the toolsmith keeps working (it only talks to me) and is not restarted;
- every new agent gets a name again (I've re-read my note on this).
